      "post": {
        "id": "ig-1790579880300-0atphf",
        "platform": "instagram",
        "imageUrl": "/media/sanctum-SAN-W2-MON-0929.png",
        "caption": "KYC packages should never train someone else's model.\n\nID docs, address proofs, corporate packs, adverse-media notes — that's customer data and bank process knowledge. Pasting it into a public or loosely governed GenAI path is not \"productivity.\" It's a control failure waiting for the next incident review.\n\nBanks don't need another generic chatbot. They need a banking-first path for document intelligence:\n\n• KYC / onboarding packages inside your boundary\n• Human review in the loop — as a feature, not a disclaimer\n• Exportable trail: what was asked, what was retrieved, which model version, who approved\n\nSanctum Assess starts with one problem. For many mid-market banks and NBFCs, that problem is KYC docs.\n\nTwo weeks. Scored. Then Prove on your data — or walk away with a clearer boundary story.\n\n→ Assess (KYC docs)\nProduct: https://www.sanctumai.us",
